    <Placemark>
      <name>Atlit-Yam (עתלית ים)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Atlit-Yam (עתלית ים)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 01. Paleolithic &amp; Epi-Paleolithic (-20000 to -10000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.2.1 (Pages 43, 44)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (01. Paleolithic &amp; Epi-Paleolithic):</b></p>
<p>An ancient well, dated to the early 6th millennium BCE (5900 BCE), found submerged 10m below current sea level. It was a cylindrical shaft 1.5m in diameter and 5.7m deep, dug through clay and into kurkar. A second well was found 100m north, dug into clay and lined with stone.</p>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#style_Paleolithic_Epipaleolithic</styleUrl>
      <ExtendedData>
        <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Atlit-Yam</value></Data>
        <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>עתלית ים</value></Data>
