    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Khirbet Jarassur (ח&apos;רבת ג&apos;אראסור)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Jarassur (ח&apos;רבת ג&apos;אראסור)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 01. Paleolithic &amp; Epi-Paleolithic (-20000 to -10000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Syria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.2.2 (Pages 44)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (01. Paleolithic &amp; Epi-Paleolithic):</b></p>
<p>A well found at a Halafian culture site (5200 BCE), considered by Campbell to be the oldest well in the world. Most of its upper part was destroyed during the excavation of an irrigation channel.</p>]]></description>
